<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47699" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tēmnos</span></b> , i, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τῆμνος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in
				Æolia</i>, now <i>Menimen</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30,
				32, § 121</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 18,
				42 al.</span></i>—Hence, ‡ </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Temni-tes</span></b> , ae,
				<i>adj. m.</i>, <i>of</i> or <i>from Temnos</i> Heraclides,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 18, 42</span></i>.—As <i>subst.</i>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tem-nītae</span></b> ,
				ārum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Temnos</i>, <i>the
			Temnites</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 19,
			45</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tem-nĭi</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Temnos</i>, <i>the
			Temnians</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 2, 47</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
